rers where appropriate."}, {"s": 181.71, "e": 185.68, "t": "These suggestions keep the person’s\nexperience in view while the team"}, {"s": 185.71, "e": 188.06, "t": "assesses and treats contributing problems."}, {"s": 188.45, "e": 193.0, "t": "For Treatment, consider falls risk\nand immediate supportive measures."}, {"s": 193.45, "e": 198.1, "t": "Fluids or oxygen may be needed,\nbut neither is an automatic response to"}, {"s": 198.13, "e": 203.14, "t": "delirium. Document delirium or\nsuspected delirium, as appropriate,"}, {"s": 203.29, "e": 205.04, "t": "and the local screening score."}, {"s": 205.23, "e": 209.9, "t": "Remember that a positive screening result\nrequires clinical assessment; it is"}, {"s": 209.93, "e": 213.0, "t": "not, on its own, a confirmed diagnosis."}, {"s": 213.45, "e": 217.06, "t": "Communicate the score and relevant\nfindings to the clinical team."}, {"s": 217.35, "e": 221.38, "t": "Inform the family and provide a delirium\nleaflet to the patient and family"}, {"s": 221.41, "e": 225.34, "t": "where appropriate. Discuss the treatment\nplan with the multidisciplinary"}, {"s": 225.37, "e": 229.92, "t": "team. Your nursing care and observations\ncomplement the work of doctors,"}, {"s": 230.15, "e": 234.42, "t": "advanced practitioners, therapists,\npharmacists, and other colleagues,"}, {"s": 234.47, "e": 236.06, "t": "according to local roles."}, {"s": 236.99, "e": 241.52, "t": "ACE-T is a set of suggestions, not an\ninstruction to do every item for every"}, {"s": 241.55, "e": 246.22, "t": "patient. Use your professional judgement\nabout what is needed, what should be"}, {"s": 246.25, "e": 248.38, "t": "added, and what is unnecessary."}, {"s": 248.81, "e": 251.2, "t": "Wording may differ by setting or country."}, {"s": 251.73, "e": 256.6, "t": "Relevant actions can be repeated during\nongoing care; treatment does not stop"}, {"s": 256.63, "e": 258.19, "t": "when four hours have passed."}, {"s": 258.53, "e": 263.32, "t": "The early pilot produc